course: dictionary
lesson: 9678
title: Words from other places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words look strange because they come from another country or language. Context still helps you. «Bolivia's official capital is Sucre, while its government sits in La Paz.» A country with two capitals sounds odd, but the words around sucre tell you it is a place, a city where the country is run from.
explain: Sucre can also be an old word for money. «The sucre was the money of Ecuador until it was replaced by the US dollar.» The word replaced tells you the sucre is no longer used. Ask yourself: what kind of word would fit here?
explain: Check whether a word is English at all. «De la farine, trois œufs, du lait et un peu de sucre» is French, not English. The sentence lists food, so sucre must be something you cook with. Start with the words you know, then guess the rest from what makes sense in that place.
fact: Sucre is the constitutional capital city of Bolivia, in South America.
fact: Bolivia's government mostly works in La Paz, so people often talk about it as having two capitals.
fact: The sucre was the money of Ecuador until the US dollar replaced it.
fact: In French, «sucre» means sugar, as in «sans sucre» (without sugar).
fact: «Sucre glace» means icing sugar, and «sucre» sounds like «SOO-kruh» to an English ear.
exercise: «Bolivia's official capital is Sucre.» What kind of word is sucre in this sentence? | A kind of animal | A colour | A sweet food | *A city
exercise: On a French food packet you read «sans sucre». What does it mean? | *Without sugar | With extra cream | Made in Paris | Sold in Ecuador
exercise: «The sucre was the money of Ecuador until it was replaced by the US dollar.» What does sucre mean here? | A tall mountain | *An old money | A type of sweet | A capital city
test: The French sentence «De la farine, trois œufs, du lait et un peu de sucre» uses sucre. What does it mean? | Salt | Flour | *Sugar | Butter
test: Why does La Paz matter in Bolivia? | *The government mostly works there | It is the old money of Ecuador | It is the French word for city | It is where the sugar is grown
exam: Jayden sees «sucre glace» on a French cake packet. What does it mean, and how did you find out? | A cold city in Ecuador, found by looking at a map | Ice cream from Bolivia, found by guessing | *Icing sugar, found by checking the words around it and the food | Brown sugar, found by counting the letters
